470 1085 #edb/ref 17592186362570 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1085 #edb/ref 17592186362576 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1085 #edb/ref 17592186362577 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1085 #edb/ref 17592186362578 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1085 #edb/ref 17592186362579 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1086 "![](images/c8/c8779f79dfa4964a94ace01d29f18a6c19bc08af804171ed2e2030a2401f3576.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows an enclosure built inside a pond. The velocity field of the water surface currents in the pond is given by $F(x,y)=⟨3x{y}^{2},\\,-{y}^{3}⟩.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1087 #uuid "d75d9fdb-caec-57de-8008-14bc25adf78a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1088 #edb/ref 17592186362570 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362472 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362474 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362476 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1069 "q-167884" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1071 "Write the space $R$ bounded by the cylinder as a type I region in three-dimensional space.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,\\le z\\le \\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$},$ where\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,1}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1072 #uuid "3dfc9372-1dd0-5243-b434-c5faa880a875" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1074 "A typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05f940e247c6cd5d862d81fc3a34658353bef5513dfe862bbc67a120c0345838.png)\n\nFirst, we have that $z$ is bounded below by $0$ and above by $3.$ So, the type I representation of $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\,}.\n$$\n\nNow, that base curve in the $xy$-plane of the cylinder's surface is the circle $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1$ centered at $(0,0).$ Therefore, the domain $D$ is given by the following disc:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,1}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362472 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362473 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362472 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362472 1077 "field-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362472 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362473 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362472 1080 #uuid "0093027b-802e-5e09-8967-82bfdc57b1f7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362473 1081 "3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362473 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362473 1084 #uuid "9fec7650-1b72-5b02-a867-aa15eec6fe97" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362475 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362474 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362474 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362474 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362475 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362474 1080 #uuid "310359c8-8da9-59ef-85bb-5493a13ee3fb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362475 1081 "0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362475 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362475 1084 #uuid "9b91d87b-b526-5ea5-9af2-8e3a561ce24d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362476 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362477 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362476 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362476 1077 "field-3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362476 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362477 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362476 1080 #uuid "57169762-8180-581f-a076-eef305161b2b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362477 1081 "\\le " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362477 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362477 1084 #uuid "d5715385-4607-5ed1-92d5-bdde6a1c0529" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362478 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362479 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362478 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362481 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362478 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362483 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362478 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362478 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362478 1069 "q-167885" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362478 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362478 1071 "The equation of the heater's surface in polar coordinates is given by $r=f(\\theta ,z),$ where $(\\theta ,z)\\in C.$ Find $f(\\theta ,z)$ and $C.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $f(\\theta ,z)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,C=[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)\\times [$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-4}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-5}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$]$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362478 1072 #uuid "e6bcccbc-6309-5897-8310-d5a4ed578985" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362478 1074 "The position of a point in cylindrical polar coordinates is written as $(r,\\theta ,z),$ where\n\n* $r\\ge 0$ and $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ are the usual plane polar coordinates, and\n\n* $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ is the usual Cartesian $z$-coordinate.\n\nThe heater is a circular cylinder of radius $3$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis.\n\nWe note the following:\n\n* Since the distance from any point on the cylinder's surface to the $z$-axis equals $3,$ we must have $r=3$ for every point on the surface.\n\n* On the other hand, $\\theta $ can vary arbitrarily in its domain, and $z$ varies arbitrarily in the domain $z\\in [0,3].$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the surface in cylindrical polar coordinates is $r=3,$ where $(\\theta ,z)\\in [0,2\\pi )\\times [0,3].$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362479 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362480 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362479 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362479 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362479 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362480 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362479 1080 #uuid "e6043475-9d1f-55c8-95bf-b782d87c62be" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362480 1081 "3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362480 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362480 1084 #uuid "05dca285-d330-53e7-9f6d-88fd0c08cd2e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362481 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362482 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362481 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362481 1077 "field-5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362481 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362482 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362481 1080 #uuid "f78dca2a-d02c-504b-ae