       \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $n(x,y)=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,i+\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,j\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,k$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362495 1072 #uuid "ed75dd18-34d6-5d52-a9e6-519946daa110" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362495 1074 "We found that a parametrization of the cylinder is given by\n\n$$\nf(\\theta ,z)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z⟩\\,(\\theta ,z)\\in C.\n$$\n\nRestricting the parametrization of the cylinder to $z=2,$ we get a parametrization $r(\\theta )$ for the heating element:\n\n$$\nr(\\theta )=f(\\theta ,2)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,2⟩\n$$\n\nFor convenience, we express $r(\\theta )$ in column vector column:\n\n$$\nr(\\theta )=[\\begin{aligned}x(\\theta ) \\\\ y(\\theta ) \\\\ z(\\theta )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nNotice that this curve is traversed *counterclockwise* when viewed from above.\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing unit normal vector to this curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1:** We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{′}(\\theta ).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(\\theta ),$ we get\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(\\theta )=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\theta ) \\\\ {y}^{′}(\\theta ) \\\\ {z}^{′}(\\theta )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Since $C$ is traversed counterclockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(\\theta )$ by $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians clockwise $(ϕ=-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nUsing the hint, the rotation matrix corresponding to a $ϕ=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ counterclockwise rotation about the $z$-axis is\n\n$$\n{R}_{z}(\\theta )=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(\\theta )$ by $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ counterclockwise, we get\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{n}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Finally, we normalize the vector found in Step 2:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||\\overset{~}{n}|| & =\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{||\\overset{~}{n}||} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}x(\\theta ) \\\\ y(\\theta ) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{3}\\,i+\\frac{y}{3}\\,j+0\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362497 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362496 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362496 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362496 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362497 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362496 1080 #uuid "1b017a4d-e67e-5487-80c5-eb76509d584e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362497 1081 "x/3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362497 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362497 1084 #uuid "71948d5e-02be-51dc-b11c-503e671f7d19" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362498 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362498 1077 "field-3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362498 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362498 1080 #uuid "d2a44b4a-6420-526a-8932-c62fb58e471c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362499 1081 "0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362499 1084 #uuid "307fd8a5-abeb-553b-a401-f90d8d28581a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362500 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362501 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362500 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362500 1077 "field-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362500 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362501 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362500 1080 #uuid "fb8df416-9cb6-541c-aa33-a5474ab16ffe" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362501 1081 "y/3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362501 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362501 1084 #uuid "220d31f3-2b87-5137-986e-02a43c004603" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362502 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362503 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362502 1069 "q-167889" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362502 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362502 1071 "Water flows over the element $E$ according to the vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=6y\\,i+x\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $E$ found in part 5 has zero $k$-component, it may be considered a two-dimensional vector defined in terms of $i$ and $j$ only. Use this to find an expression for the flux of $F$ across the element in terms of $x$ and $y.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Flux = \n${∮}_{E}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\text{d}s.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362502 1072 #uuid "9d35a688-8b95-5b4b-a5d5-a0c9f931f061" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362502 1074 "If $F$ is a vector field and $E$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $E$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{E}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit vector to $E.$\n\n![](images/2c/2cd5e4c7ab86cdb999e239e986713a51c07b8decb629b1ee4a656077590f04bb.png)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{E}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{E}(6y\\,i+x\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{x}{3}\\,i+\\frac{y}{3}\\,j)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={∮}_{E}2xy+\\frac{1}{3}xy\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={∮}_{E}\\frac{7}{3}xy\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362504 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362503 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362503 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362503 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362504 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362503 1080 #uuid "47f7b160-4a23-58c9-94a1-d65bba0f866a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362504 1081 "\\frac{7}{3}xy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362504 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362504 1084 #uuid "0368d3ef-7ff9-5da6-857d-96776c228a1d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362505 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362506 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362505 1069 "q-167890" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362505 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362505 1071 "Evaluate the integral in step 6 to find the flux of $F$ across the element.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Flux = \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362505 1072 #uuid "04b077f7-c06e-58b2-a427-71541763f158" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362505 1074 "We will evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{E}\\frac{7}{3}xy\\,\\text{d}s\n$$\n\nfound in step 6 using the formula\n\n$$\n{∮}_{E}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(\\theta ))\\,‖{r}^{′}(\\theta )‖\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nwith the parametrization of the curve $E$ given by\n\n$$\nr(\\theta )=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nAs we found previously, ${r}^{′}(\\theta )=⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||{r}^{′}(\\theta )|| & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=\\frac{7}{3}xy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(\\theta )) & =\\frac{7}{3}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =21\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{E}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(\\theta ))\\,‖{r}^{′}(\\theta )‖\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }21\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot 3\\cdot \\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =63{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta . \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{63}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\frac{63}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{63}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{63}{4}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362506 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362507 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362506 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362506 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362506 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362507 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362506 1080 #uuid "888db239-13fc-5af3-9362-ec8dfd52191e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362507 1081 "0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362507 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362507 1084 #uuid "2913f404-2728-588d-a659-7b2224909a8b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362508 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362509 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362508 1069 "q-168534" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362508 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362508 1071 "![](images/b7/b7d9cf2ef89d1a21cd9062a9ef1e709fb1c98bfc7de75b6b0447a204bd8472fc.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            After some time, the duct's settings are changed. The diagram above shows the flow of air induced at the top of a room in the $xy$-plane around the duct's outlet. The velocity field $F$ in this plane is given by\n\n$$\nF=({x}^{2}-2{y}^{2})\\,\\text{i}-2xy\\,\\text{j}.\n$$\n\nFind the flux of the airflow across the boundary $C$ of the exit of the tube.\n\n*Hint: First check if $F$ is source-free.*\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The required flux is $\\,{∮}_{C}^{}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362508 1072 #uuid "99f7e2de-e770-5564-a4da-4aa6a0cb3a35" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362508 1074 "Recall that, if $F=P\\,\\text{i}+Q\\,\\text{j}$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2},$ then the following are equivalent:\n\n* $F$ is a source-free vector field.\n\n* $∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.$\n\n* The flux ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s$ along any closed curve $C\\in D$ is zero.\n\n* Flux is path-independent. That is, given two curves ${C}_{1},{C}_{2}\\in D$ with the same start and end points, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n* There exists a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ for $F.$\n\nFirst, for our vector field $F=({x}^{2}-2{y}^{2})\\,\\text{i}-2xy\\,\\text{j}$, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2xy) \\\\  & =2x-2x \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $F$ is a source-free vector field. So, the flux of $F$ across any closed curve is zero. Hence,\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362510 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362509 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362509 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362509 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362510 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362509 1080 #uuid "6f03ccc6-c5e8-5fa0-bc8f-340057c238c3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362510 1081 "0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362510 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362510 1084 #uuid "edc2c8d2-e408-55b6-aaaf-5d6de174ca1a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362511 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362512 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362511 1069 "q-168558" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362511 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362511 1071 "Use Green's theorem to write down a double integral that gives the circulation of $F$ along $C,$ transversed counterclockwise.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362511 1072 #uuid "076b553d-9b94-5414-af96-ed5daed9cd1c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362511 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](images/46/4693916207540a6453c6c3775824ba577e62fea0a18b07e96f8814901d9ad80e.png)\n\nFirst, notice that we can rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}({x}^{2}-2{y}^{2})\\,dx+(-2xy)\\,dy\n$$\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)=-2xy.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-4y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2y-(-4y))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2y\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362512 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362513 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362512 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362512 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362512 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362513 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362512 1080 #uuid "e9a9ee48-7978-5cd0-a274-d255560a0858" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362513 1081 "2y" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362513 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362513 1084 #uuid "19d912c2-2ff0-503a-91db-848ccbab9dca" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362514 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362515 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362514 1069 "q-168622" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362514 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362514 1071 "Find the circulation $Γ$ of the the airflow $F$ along $C.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $Γ=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362514 1072 #uuid "989d7acd-67a4-5cd1-9dd4-46407f1429c8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362514 1074 "The circulation $Γ$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nFrom step 6, we can write this as the following repeated integral:\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =x{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(2-0)(4-0) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362515 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362516 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362515 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362515 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362515 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362516 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362515 1080 #uuid "5cc5ee0d-3989-5ee4-951c-b1c8dfa52add" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362516 1081 "8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362516 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362516 1084 #uuid "f43f8492-131e-5e50-a4a6-cb5d33c90b70" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362518 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362520 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362522 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362524 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362526 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362528 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1069 "q-168623" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1071 "![](images/1a/1ae6fd567aa4a7ce40a47e64e682bf2e908ab503e400bf47c27df06f87a57a96.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            Write the solid $R$ bounded by the duct $S$ as a type I region in three-dimensional space.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,\\le z\\le \\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$},$ where\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,\\le x\\le \\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-4}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-5}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,\\le y\\le \\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-6}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1072 #uuid "f2b6fda7-6380-5eb1-8d62-3733e9b76fdd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362517 1074 "A typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05f940e247c6cd5d862d81fc3a34658353bef5513dfe862bbc67a120c0345838.png)\n\nFirst, the projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xy$-plane gives the domain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n* the *bottom* surface $z={f}_{1}(x,y)=0,$ and\n\n* the *top* surface $z={f}_{2}(x,y)=4.$\n\n![](images/69/69faebe379efc8a012346b8aba235edca8e9d5adabd3bb52b5009c20d73de655.png)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,0\\le z\\le 4\\,}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362519 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362518 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362518 1077 "field-5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362518 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362519 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362518 1080 #uuid "8fd46772-1b66-594b-8bb2-513fbac113dc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362519 1081 "0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362519 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362519 1084 #uuid "2e96de77-9cbf-59f3-aaeb-d524f8048620" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362520 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362521 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362520 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362520 1077 "field-6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362520 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362521 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362520 1080 #uuid "2358e1cb-5ddd-5a91-96dd-2c895185338a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362521 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362521 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362521 1084 #uuid "0c83c3b5-b22c-5ab3-9676-35fb5775b76c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362523 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362522 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362522 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362522 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362523 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362522 1080 #uuid "57092d3e-1eda-551b-8ed2-7fd22e107d30" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362523 1081 "0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362523 1083 #edb/ref 1759